{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#931","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#931","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#931\",\"parent_revision\":\"da15cb29f42aa2fc949aa390141603db2780dbae\",\"root_revision\":\"740b83aabd418e25105188374851fd6bf4fdbf4e7a2e0c8eff7a3c395bed1737\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSave active milestone number, current wave, dispatch plan path, and active team member IDs before context compaction. Restore by pointing to dispatch plan file on session resume. Enables long /work-milestone sessions to survive compaction. Pattern sourced from Citadel pre-compact.js.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | PreCompact hook event supported | DERIVABLE | Check Claude Code hook events (see #1034 for PreCompact docs gap) |\\n| 2 | `work-milestone` skill location | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/` or similar |\\n| 3 | Citadel pre-compact.js pattern | AVAILABLE | Named in item as source reference |\\n| 4 | How to detect active milestone from hook context | MISSING | Hook receives limited context \u2014 must verify what state is available |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 requires confirming what state a PreCompact hook can access about the active session. If milestone state is not accessible from hook context, architecture changes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **compact preservation for milestone sessions** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Citadel assessment .claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Medium complexity. Depends on PreCompact hook capabilities verification.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A PreCompact hook (`.claude/hooks/`) saves milestone state to `plan/milestone-{N}-state.json` before compaction\\n- State includes: milestone number, current wave index, dispatch plan path, active team member IDs\\n- On session resume, `/work-milestone resume` reads the state file and restores orchestration context\\n- State file is overwritten on each PreCompact event (idempotent)\\n- If no active milestone, hook exits without writing\\n- Pattern adapted from Citadel pre-compact.js\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `.claude/hooks/milestone-precompact.cjs` \u2014 new PreCompact hook\\n- `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 register hook\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/` \u2014 add `resume` command handling\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a /work-milestone session user running long parallel executions, I need active milestone state (milestone number, current wave, dispatch plan path, active team member IDs) saved before context compaction so the session can resume without losing orchestration state.\\n\",\"digest\":\"a3228429280abfe6752f0320d4fc0eaff5a880336d7cb5727611b0df3bd184fb\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgySiw\"}"}